{
  "_id": "3JmL9hprwqQ2T059DrT7q9kzfSO",
  "_type": "Doc",
  "_index": "a5V",
  "title": "Button",
  "navigationTitle": "",
  "body": [
    {
      "_type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "Triggers an action. Buttons come in solid, outline, ghost and link variants, in five colors and with sizes for toolbars and icon-only buttons."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "ComponentExampleBlock",
      "_id": "3JmL9fgLj37Jan06A2kxiF4XiuI",
      "example": "Button"
    },
    {
      "_type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "Variants"
        }
      ],
      "_anchor": "variants"
    },
    {
      "_type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "Solid is the default. Use outline for secondary actions, ghost inside toolbars and dense rows, and link for an action that sits in a line of text."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "ComponentExampleBlock",
      "_id": "3JmL9gUihA69TA3qrrt6bt0GmfW",
      "example": "ButtonVariants"
    },
    {
      "_type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "Colors"
        }
      ],
      "_anchor": "colors"
    },
    {
      "_type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "Primary marks the main action of a screen. Destructive and warning are for actions that remove or overwrite content."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "ComponentExampleBlock",
      "_id": "3JmL9cQSZRxSOsA5VB9idgpl8ji",
      "example": "ButtonColors"
    },
    {
      "_type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "Sizes"
        }
      ],
      "_anchor": "sizes"
    },
    {
      "_type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "Small fits toolbars and table rows, large suits empty states. The icon sizes render a square button without a label: give it an `aria-label`."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "ComponentExampleBlock",
      "_id": "3JmL9cPYEhfZP39UwGsq3a8YEbp",
      "example": "ButtonSizes"
    },
    {
      "_type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "Icons and loading"
        }
      ],
      "_anchor": "icons-and-loading"
    },
    {
      "_type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "Pass an icon component to show it before the label. While `loading` is set the button shows a spinner and can't be pressed again."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "ComponentExampleBlock",
      "_id": "3JmL9dcvK1yGeiAUW0dziXHMvSY",
      "example": "ButtonIcons"
    },
    {
      "_type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "Props"
        }
      ],
      "_anchor": "props"
    },
    {
      "_type": "ComponentPropsBlock",
      "_id": "3JmL9co2rH0X4lVqnPidHLb1v4R",
      "component": "Button"
    },
    {
      "_type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "Accessibility"
        }
      ],
      "_anchor": "accessibility"
    },
    {
      "_type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "Built on the React Aria button: it responds to Enter and Space, shows a focus ring for keyboard users only and handles presses the same way for mouse, touch and keyboard. With `asChild` the styling moves onto its child, such as a link, which then takes care of its own semantics."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
